# Gameplay observation for inc-30ps: does a creature standing between the
# player and the player's chosen target eat a Magic Missile cast at that
# target, or does the missile reach the creature actually chosen?
#
# Run identically against the pre-epic tree (master, commit d228dd2) and the
# inc-30ps branch tip, same seed, same options file, separate run dirs:
#
#   cd /Users/brianhill/Scripts/Incursion-baseline
#   INCURSION_OPTIONS=tools/fixtures/options-2026-08-22.dat \
#   INCURSION_RUN_DIR=logs/runs/lof-mm-before \
#       tools/headless.sh docs/evidence/inc-30ps/lof-magic-missile.keys 1
#
#   cd /Users/brianhill/Scripts/Incursion-inc-30ps
#   INCURSION_OPTIONS=tools/fixtures/options-2026-08-22.dat \
#   INCURSION_RUN_DIR=logs/runs/lof-mm-after \
#       tools/headless.sh docs/evidence/inc-30ps/lof-magic-missile.keys 1
#
# SETUP, all via wizard mode, following the pattern already proven in
# tools/keys/minor-drain-touch.keys and tools/keys/school-focus.keys:
#   * Freeze Monsters (Wizard Mode Switches row 11) stops either goblin
#     acting on its own, so only the player's own cast moves HP.
#   * Learn Any Spell grants Magic Missile as an innate spell (no spellbook,
#     no mana-pool math needed).
#   * Monster Summoning places a goblin ONE square east of the player, then
#     Make Player Master of Monster converts that specific goblin (the only
#     candidate onscreen at that moment, so the RIGHT ENTER pick is
#     unambiguous) into the player's own companion -- an ally, not a bystander.
#   * A second Monster Summoning places a second, still-hostile goblin TWO
#     squares east of the player -- directly behind the ally, on the same
#     line.
#
# TARGETING. Magic Missile's own qval is bare Q_TAR (lib/wspells.irh), so
# casting it opens the ring-based target cursor (src/Term.cpp EffectPrompt,
# typ == Q_TAR branch), not a free-moving location cursor. The cursor starts
# on the player; the first RIGHT press aims strictly east and lands on the
# NEAREST candidate in that direction (the ally, one square away); the second
# RIGHT press advances the cursor along the ring to the next candidate on the
# same bearing, which BearingCompare (src/Term.cpp) orders by distance when
# two things share a bearing -- so it lands on the hostile goblin two squares
# away. This was confirmed empirically before writing this script: pressing
# 'w' at each cursor position (the wizard "dump whatever the cursor is on"
# feature, src/Term.cpp:2361-2388) printed X:83 Y:13 after one RIGHT and
# X:84 Y:13 after two, i.e. the ally then the hostile, on a player standing
# at X:82 Y:13. ENTER at that point fires at the hostile goblin -- the
# creature actually chosen, with the ally standing in the way.
#
# THE ORACLE is each creature's own HP line from Player::BrowseThings /
# Creature::Dump ("Examine Nearby Things" in the wizard menu), read before and
# after the cast. It cycles through nearby things with RIGHT and prints the
# raw cHP/mHP field, along with the thing's X/Y, so the two goblins are
# identified by position rather than by list order.
#
# A run against the PRE-EPIC tree is expected to show the ally's HP fall and
# the hostile's HP untouched -- the ally, one square closer, eats the shot
# meant for the creature the player actually selected. A run against the
# branch is expected to show the reverse: the ally untouched, the hostile
# struck.

@include ../../../tools/keys/chargen-mage.keys
ESC

w
y
@choose "Wizard Mode Switches"
DOWN*10
SPACE
ESC

w
@choose "Learn Any Spell"
"Magic Missile"
ENTER

w
@choose "Monster Summoning"
@choose "Goblinkin"
@choose "goblin"
RIGHT ENTER
@dump:ally-summoned

w
@choose "Make Player Master of Monster"
RIGHT ENTER
@dump:ally-converted

w
@choose "Monster Summoning"
@choose "Goblinkin"
@choose "goblin"
RIGHT RIGHT ENTER
@dump:hostile-summoned

w
@choose "Examine Nearby Things"
@dump:before-player
RIGHT
@dump:before-1
RIGHT
@dump:before-2
ESC

m
@choose "Magic Missile"
RIGHT
RIGHT
ENTER
@while "more --" SPACE
@dump:after-cast

w
@choose "Examine Nearby Things"
@dump:after-player
RIGHT
@dump:after-1
RIGHT
@dump:after-2
ESC

@quit
